 34SI dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 29-May-2026)          
 34SI c  2002En02: a 73-MeV {+35}Si secondary beam was produced via             
 34SI2c  fragmentation of 100-MeV/nucleon 40Ar primary beam on a 9Be target,    
 34SI3c  separated by the NSCL A1200 fragment separator, and impinged on a      
 34SI4c  93-mg/cm2 9Be secondary target. The reaction residues were analyzed    
 34SI5c  using the S800 spectrograph. |g rays from the reaction residues were   
 34SI6c  detected using an array of 38 NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,    
 34SI7c  |g|g-coin, and (residual)|g-coin. Comparisons with shell-model         
 34SI8c  calculations.                                                          
 34SI c  2002En02 fits their |g spectrum using known 34Al |b-delayed |g rays    
 34SI2c  from 2001Nu01. 2002En02 states that an unambiguous placement of the |g 
 34SI3c  rays from 2001Nu01 is not always possible, neither is there a          
 34SI4c  one-to-one correspondence between the proposed excited states and the  
 34SI5c  shell-model calculation. A disagreement between the overall fit and the
 34SI6c  measured data is clearly visible and indicates the possibility of an   
 34SI7c  even more complex spectrum.                                            
